libgcc — GCC's own runtime source, linked into the game as a library
=====================================================================

Why this directory exists
-------------------------
Some of the game binary is GCC's runtime library (libgcc.a), linked in by the
original toolchain. That code is GCC source under the GNU GPL, and its runtime
exception covers LINKING a compiled library into a program, not copying its
source text into this project's own .c files. So it lives here, verbatim and
under its own licence, and the build compiles it and links it as a library
(operator decision, claudiverse RULING #8206; design: PROCEDURE #8224; member
list by address: NOTE #8217). It is never transcribed into a game .c file.

Nothing in the GCC files below is edited. If a member's verbatim source does
not compile to the ROM's bytes, that member stays INCLUDE_ASM in its game unit;
the source is never changed to make it match.

